# Integration Repository Mode (Cursor Component Factory)

Follow:
- `fast-workflow/CORE_WORKFLOW.md`;
- `fast-workflow/INTEGRATION_REPO_WORKFLOW.md`.

Before editing, identify:
- Target integration edge (`<consumer>` → `<provider>`);
- Old and new versions (both must have verified `Ready` status);
- Approved contract schema version (`contracts/`);
- Integration scenario (`scenarios/` or `product/features/`);
- Allowed paths: dependency manifest and `tests/integration/<edge>/`.

## Scope & Boundaries

- Modify only the integration repository / root application manifest.
- Update exactly **one** published dependency per iteration.
- Treat component source code as read-only.
- Test at least one successful path (Happy Path) and one expected failure (Error Handling).
- Record `Integrated` in the registry (`integrations/status.*`) **only after explicit human approval**.

## Prohibitions

- Do not edit component source code.
- Do not update unrelated dependencies or edges in the same task.
- Do not substitute an unpublished local build without an approved `Ready` release/tag.
- Do not automatically patch both sides of an incompatibility.

## Handling Incompatibilities & Breaking Changes

On mismatch or test failure:
1. Stop the integration iteration immediately.
2. Do not hot-patch code in the integration repo.
3. Report expected behavior, actual behavior, affected consumers, and the component repository that owns the fix.

When recording `Integrated`, synchronously update `integrations/status.*` and `README.md` (integrated edges, component versions, environment startup, E2E test commands).
